1
00:00:06,021 --> 00:00:10,112
A flame gives light. But the light
is not a second thing sent out.

2
00:00:10,192 --> 00:00:11,392
It is the burning.

3
00:00:12,206 --> 00:00:15,645
The Dzogchen tradition has a
term for this kind of appearing:

4
00:00:15,725 --> 00:00:18,390
lhun grub, spontaneous presence.

5
00:00:18,470 --> 00:00:20,156
The word carries a risk.

6
00:00:20,236 --> 00:00:22,344
It can slide into causelessness.

7
00:00:22,424 --> 00:00:28,159
And an uncaused source is exactly
the svabhāva that Madhyamaka rejects:

8
00:00:28,239 --> 00:00:30,292
a nature that stands on its own.

9
00:00:30,372 --> 00:00:32,525
The risk is best named openly.

10
00:00:33,341 --> 00:00:37,242
To keep the two traditions
aligned, separate two questions.

11
00:00:37,322 --> 00:00:39,850
The first asks how an
appearance comes about.

12
00:00:39,930 --> 00:00:41,834
Every appearance has an answer.

13
00:00:41,914 --> 00:00:46,712
It arises from causes and conditions,
and the Middle Way analysis works at that

14
00:00:46,792 --> 00:00:50,570
level. The second asks about
the nature of what appears.

15
00:00:50,650 --> 00:00:56,250
That nature is emptiness: the absence
of any existence from its own side.

16
00:00:56,330 --> 00:00:59,062
And emptiness is not confined to mind.

17
00:00:59,142 --> 00:01:02,296
There is not one thing that
has not arisen dependently.

18
00:01:02,376 --> 00:01:04,800
So there is not one
thing that is not empty.

19
00:01:05,601 --> 00:01:10,561
Spontaneous presence, then, is not
an extra ingredient sitting on top of

20
00:01:10,641 --> 00:01:11,689
emptiness.

21
00:01:11,769 --> 00:01:15,575
In this book's reading, it is what
dependent origination looks like from the

22
00:01:15,655 --> 00:01:20,086
inside. It is what remains once
every demand for a producer,

23
00:01:20,166 --> 00:01:23,075
substrate or ultimate why has run out.

24
00:01:23,155 --> 00:01:26,309
Dependent arising is the
analytic description.

25
00:01:26,389 --> 00:01:31,485
Spontaneous presence is the experiential
description of the same appearing.

26
00:01:31,565 --> 00:01:33,795
What presents is already complete.

27
00:01:33,875 --> 00:01:36,336
Both deny production by an essence.

28
00:01:36,416 --> 00:01:38,365
Both leave appearance intact.

29
00:01:39,194 --> 00:01:43,082
The phrase "no why or because"
is worth returning to.

30
00:01:43,162 --> 00:01:45,405
It does not deny that causes work.

31
00:01:45,485 --> 00:01:47,593
In ordinary life, "why?"

32
00:01:47,673 --> 00:01:49,834
is a perfectly usable question.

33
00:01:49,914 --> 00:01:53,598
What the phrase denies is a
ground beneath the regularity:

34
00:01:53,678 --> 00:01:57,660
a reason why it is so,
which is itself uncaused.

35
00:01:57,740 --> 00:01:59,658
There the question stops applying.

36
00:01:59,738 --> 00:02:03,843
Not because the answer is hidden, but
because there was never a ground to ask

37
00:02:03,923 --> 00:02:05,123
about.

38
00:02:05,574 --> 00:02:08,714
Two safeguards keep this
from becoming a new ground.

39
00:02:08,794 --> 00:02:13,062
Emptiness is not a separate
reality standing behind things.

40
00:02:13,142 --> 00:02:16,704
And emptiness must not become
a hidden substrate either,

41
00:02:16,784 --> 00:02:19,439
because emptiness is itself empty.

42
00:02:20,253 --> 00:02:23,542
Together, these point to
something easy to miss.

43
00:02:23,622 --> 00:02:27,686
Appearance and its conditions
do not stand in a hierarchy.

44
00:02:27,766 --> 00:02:30,349
The conditions are not
a ground beneath it.

45
00:02:30,429 --> 00:02:34,222
The appearance is not a surface
expressing something deeper.

46
00:02:34,302 --> 00:02:38,257
Neither rules the other, because
neither has a place to rule from.

47
00:02:38,337 --> 00:02:39,996
The arrangement is flat.

48
00:02:40,076 --> 00:02:42,523
The chariot's parts and the chariot.

49
00:02:42,603 --> 00:02:44,425
A flame and its fuel.

50
00:02:44,505 --> 00:02:46,423
A seeing and its object.

51
00:02:46,503 --> 00:02:51,264
Each occurs within the same web,
with none presiding over the rest.

52
00:02:52,081 --> 00:02:54,052
And this flatness has no owner.

53
00:02:54,132 --> 00:02:56,389
To ask "whose appearance is this?"

54
00:02:56,469 --> 00:02:59,052
assumes someone standing
behind the appearing.

55
00:02:59,132 --> 00:03:03,808
That someone is not found, and the
appearing does not stop for want of one.

56
00:03:03,888 --> 00:03:07,490
It appears of itself,
but only in a thin sense.

57
00:03:07,570 --> 00:03:10,846
The coming together of
conditions is the appearing,

58
00:03:10,926 --> 00:03:13,296
as the flame's light is the burning.

59
00:03:14,198 --> 00:03:19,037
"Of itself" means only that the appearance
is not borrowed from somewhere else.

60
00:03:19,117 --> 00:03:21,075
It names no self that owns it.

61
00:03:21,155 --> 00:03:25,110
Conditions are not little agents,
each with a point of view.

62
00:03:25,190 --> 00:03:29,367
And "own" is where a self
most easily slips back in.

63
00:03:30,190 --> 00:03:33,833
The Middle Way verses look for a
self apart from the aggregates,

64
00:03:33,913 --> 00:03:37,352
the bundles of body and
mind, and find none.

65
00:03:37,432 --> 00:03:40,042
What is left is only to
see what appearing is,

66
00:03:40,122 --> 00:03:41,772
once the search has ended.

67
00:03:42,589 --> 00:03:45,312
It appears. And it belongs to no one.

